<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Constantine I</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Constantine the Great, Emperor Constantine I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Constantine I, known as Constantine the Great, was Roman emperor in the early fourth century CE. He was the first emperor to convert to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> and legalised the faith throughout the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a>. He refounded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantion">Byzantion</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, which became the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/constantine-i.jpg" alt="Constantine I" width="293" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Merulana · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Statua_di_Costantino_ai_musei_capitolini.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
